# Lazymap Directory Structure

├── lazymap.sh - main
├── extra
│   ├── responder.sh - Manages the execution of Responder.
│   └── wordlists
│       └── kerberos_users.txt - Default username list for Kerberos enumeration.
├── lib
│   ├── checks.sh - Functions for checking dependencies and input validation.
│   ├── compat.sh - Bash 3.x compatibility helpers (option store, ordered tables, array utils).
│   ├── installer.sh - Detects the package manager and installs missing tools.
│   ├── colors.sh - Handles the output colors.
│   ├── help.sh - Displays the help message.
│   └── state.sh - Resume state tracking, run time reporting and interrupt handling.
│── scans
│   ├── live_hosts.sh - Handles live host discovery to find online targets for scans.
│   ├── dns.sh - Conducts DNS related vulnerability checks.
│   ├── ldap.sh - Performs LDAP anonymous bind scan.
│   ├── metasploit.sh - Runs Metasploit scans for RDP, RPC, Oracle, NTP, SNMP, AFP and Kerberos username enumeration.
│   ├── nmap.sh - Manages all Nmap scans.
│   ├── pret.sh - Manages PRET printer security checks.
│   ├── smb.sh - Contains crackmapexec for SMBv1 scan and Unauthenticated RPC scans.
│   └── web.sh - Handles web and SSH related scans.
├── reports
    ├── html_report.sh - Generates an HTML report from overall scan results.
    └── send_discord_webhook.sh - Sends the zipped results to a Discord webhook.
